<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isonokami Shrine</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isonokami Jingū</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isonokami Shrine is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinto">Shinto</a> shrine in Tenri, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> Prefecture, one of the oldest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. It was associated with the Mononobe clan, who kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamato-court">Yamato court</a>'s weapons, and served as an armoury of sacred swords. Among its treasures is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-branched-sword">Seven-Branched Sword</a>, a gift from a Baekje king to a ruler of Wa, now a National Treasure of Japan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isonokami-shrine.jpg" alt="Isonokami Shrine" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fg2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isonokami.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
